(56,'dwmarsden','Marsden, David','David W. Marsden',NULL,'white','male','David W. Marsden represents Virginia Senate District 37 as a Democrat, and took office in January 2010. Born in Northern Virginia, Marsden graduated from W.T. Woodson High School in 1966 and earned his degree from Randolph-Macon College in 1970. He worked as a Probation Officer with the Fairfax County Juvenile and Domestic Relations Court and served as the first Superintendent of the Fairfax County Juvenile Detention Center for seventeen years. Marsden served as Legislative Aide to Virginia House Delegate Jim Dillard beginning in 1999 and was appointed Chief Deputy and Acting Director of the Virginia Department of Juvenile Justice by Governor Jim Gilmore in 2000. He served in the Virginia House of Delegates before his election to the Senate in a 2010 special election. He resides in Burke with his wife, Julia.','2006-11-19 15:09:59','2026-01-06 02:11:30'),
