(269,'rcdeeds','Deeds, Creigh','R. Creigh Deeds',NULL,'white','male','R. Creigh Deeds represents Virginia Senate District 11 as a Democrat, and took office in January 2001. Born in Richmond in 1958, Deeds was raised in Bath County and graduated from Concord College in 1980 and Wake Forest University School of Law in 1984. He practiced as an attorney and served as Commonwealth\'s Attorney of Bath County before his election to the Virginia House of Delegates in 1992, where he served until 2001. Deeds currently serves as Chair of the Senate Commerce and Labor Committee and sits on the Courts of Justice, Finance and Appropriations, Privileges and Elections, and Rules committees. He resides in Charlottesville with his wife, Siobhan.','0000-00-00 00:00:00','2026-01-06 02:11:30'),
