(278,'melocke','Locke, Mamie','Mamie E. Locke',NULL,'black','female','Mamie E. Locke represents Virginia Senate District 23 as a Democrat, and took office in January 2004. Born in Brandon, Mississippi, in 1954, Locke earned a Bachelor of Arts from Tougaloo College, a Master of Arts and Ph.D. from Atlanta University, and certificates in Management Development from Harvard University and Archives Administration from Emory University. She is a Professor Emeritus of Political Science at Hampton University and served as Mayor of Hampton from 2000 to 2004 and on the Hampton City Council from 1996 to 2000. She resides in Hampton.','0000-00-00 00:00:00','2026-01-06 02:11:30'),
(279,'lllucas','Lucas, Louise','L. Louise Lucas',NULL,'black','female','Louise L. Lucas represents Virginia Senate District 18 as a Democrat, and took office in January 1992. Lucas resides in Portsmouth.','0000-00-00 00:00:00','2026-01-06 02:11:30'),
