(282,'rtmcdougle','McDougle, Ryan','Ryan T. McDougle',NULL,'white','male','Ryan T. McDougle represents Virginia Senate District 26 as a Republican, and took office in January 2006. Born in Hanover in 1971, McDougle earned a Bachelor of Science in Political Science and History from James Madison University and a Juris Doctor from the Marshall-Wythe School of Law at The College of William and Mary. He practices as an attorney and served in the Virginia House of Delegates from 2002 to 2006 before his election to the Senate. He currently serves as Senate Minority Leader. He resides in Mechanicsville with his wife, Robyn.','0000-00-00 00:00:00','2026-01-06 02:11:31'),
