(286,'mdobenshain','Obenshain, Mark','Mark D. Obenshain',NULL,'white','male','Mark D. Obenshain represents Virginia Senate District 2 as a Republican, and took office in January 2004. Born in Richmond in 1962, Obenshain graduated from Virginia Tech in 1984 with a Bachelor of Arts and earned his Juris Doctor from Washington and Lee University School of Law in 1987. He is a Principal with Obenshain Law Group and served on the Board of Visitors at James Madison University from 1995 to 2003. He resides in Rockingham County with his wife, Suzanne.','0000-00-00 00:00:00','2026-01-06 02:11:30'),
