(307,'rsnortham','Northam, Ralph','Ralph S. Northam','1959-09-13','white','male','Pediatric neurologist at Children\'s Hospital of the King\'s Daughters. Eastern Shore native. VMI graduate. U.S. Army veteran.','2007-11-17 16:08:18','2014-01-19 17:33:27'),
(308,'jhvogel','Vogel, Jill Holtzman','Jill Holtzman Vogel',NULL,'white','female','Shenandoah Valley native. Practicing campaign finance attorney. One of the team of attorneys who represented the Bush-Cheney campaign in the Florida recount in 2000. Former Chief Counsel of the Republican National Committee. Received her BA in government and religion from William and Mary and her JD from DePaul University. Married with four children.','2007-11-17 16:16:12','2023-12-30 01:53:21'),
(309,'rhstuart','Stuart, Richard','Richard H. Stuart',NULL,'white','male','Richard H. Stuart represents Virginia Senate District 25 as a Republican, and took office in January 2008. Born in Fredericksburg in 1964, Stuart earned a Bachelor of Arts from Virginia Wesleyan College and a Juris Doctor from the T.C. Williams School of Law. He practices as an attorney and served as chairman of the FOIA Advisory Council. He resides in Westmoreland County with his wife, Lisa.','2007-11-17 17:44:40','2026-01-06 02:11:31'),
(310,'jcpetersen','Petersen, Chap','John Chapman Petersen','1968-03-27','white','male','Attorney practicing business law with Surovell, Markle, Isaacs & Levy, PLC. Fairfax native. Elected to Fairfax City Council in 1998. Member of the House of Delegates from 2001-5, resigned his seat to seek unsuccessfully the Democratic nomination for Lt. Governor. Graduate of the University of Virginia and Williams College. Married with three children.','2007-11-17 17:46:48','2023-12-24 02:56:21'),
(311,'glbarker','Barker, George','George L. Barker','1951-08-24','white','male','Associate director of the Health Systems Agency of Northern Virginia. Holds a BA and an MS from Harvard. Married with two grown children.','2007-11-17 17:58:05','2023-12-30 01:53:21'),
(312,'pfnichols','Nichols, Paul','Paul F. Nichols','1952-03-27','white','male','Attorney. From Pennsylvania. Holds degrees from Kings College and George Mason University. Has two grown children.','2007-11-17 18:09:30','2020-02-15 02:19:18'),
(313,'mgvanderhye','Vanderhye, Margi','Margaret G. Vanderhye',NULL,'white','female','Government affairs consultant. Former assistant to Henry Kissinger and Brent Scowcroft at the National Security Council. Holds degrees from Northwestern University and Johns Hopkins. Graduate of the Sorensen Institute for Political Leadership. Married with two grown children.','2007-11-17 18:29:26','2020-02-15 02:19:18'),
