(322,'jcmiller','Miller, John','John C. Miller','1947-12-09','white','male','Vice President of University Relations at Christopher Newport. Prior to that he was a news anchor at WVEC for six years, news director of the same station for twelve years, and administrative assistant to U.S. Sen. Paul Trible for six years.  Got his BS and ED from Northern Illinois University. Married with two grown children.','2007-11-21 22:50:58','2020-02-15 02:19:18'),
(323,'rksmith','Smith, Ralph','Ralph K. Smith','1942-07-19','white','male','Retired from the trailer part manufacturing business. Served as the mayor of Roanoke from 2000-4. Defeated Sen. Brandon Bell in the Republican primary. Graduate of Nashville Auto-Diesel College. Has four children.','2007-11-21 23:02:33','2020-02-15 02:19:18'),
(324,'acpollard','Pollard, Albert','Albert C. Pollard, Jr.','1967-09-18','white','male','Pollard held the seat from 2000-2005 before stepping down and running (unsuccessfully) for state senate, though regained his seat after his replacement won election to the U.S. House of Representatives.\r\n\r\nHe holds a degree in urban planning from Virginia Commonwealth University. Pollard is married and has three young children.','2008-02-20 19:10:46','2020-02-15 02:19:18'),
