(342,'sasurovell','Surovell, Scott','Scott A. Surovell',NULL,'white','male','Scott A. Surovell represents Virginia Senate District 34 as a Democrat, and took office in January 2016. A twelfth-generation Virginian and lifelong Mount Vernon resident, Surovell graduated magna cum laude from James Madison University in 1993 with a Bachelor of Arts in Political Science and earned his Juris Doctor from the University of Virginia School of Law in 1996. He is a co-founding partner of Surovell Isaacs & Levy PLC, a law firm in Fairfax. Surovell served in the Virginia House of Delegates from 2010 to 2016 before his election to the Senate, where he chairs the Courts of Justice Committee and serves on the Finance and Appropriations, Commerce and Labor, Rehabilitation and Social Services, and Rules committees. He resides in Mount Vernon.','2009-12-03 22:13:05','2026-01-06 02:11:30'),
(343,'letorian','Torian, Luke','Luke E. Torian',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2009-12-03 22:13:10','2026-02-13 17:43:08'),
(344,'ravillanueva','Villanueva, Ron','Ronald A. Villanueva','1970-03-30','asian','male','The former member of the Virginia Beach City Council holds a degree from Old Dominion University. He\'s a former member of the Coast Guard Reserve, and owns <a href=\"http://www.seksolutions.com/\">a small office supply contractor</a>.','2009-12-03 22:13:15','2018-01-10 02:58:53'),
(345,'jlmcwaters','McWaters, Jeff','Jeffrey L. McWaters',NULL,'white','male','Elected in a special election, held the night prior to the beginning of the 2010 General Assembly session. The election was held because the incumbent, Sen. Ken Stolle, won the seat of sheriff in Virginia Beach in the November election.','2010-01-13 19:50:37','2020-02-15 02:19:18'),
(346,'raabbott','Abbott, Robin','Robin A. Abbott','1953-01-20','white','female','Abbott is an attorney, a mother of four, and holds degrees from Christopher Newport University and William & Mary.','2010-01-17 22:10:57','2020-02-15 02:19:18'),
(347,'mjames','James, Matthew','Matthew James','1955-09-11','black','male','James is the president of a regional workforce development organization. He holds a bachelor\'s degree in economics from Hampton University and an MBA from Northwestern University. He is married with two grown daughters.','2010-01-18 12:31:38','2020-02-15 02:19:18'),
