(376,'bafavola','Favola, Barbara','Barbara A. Favola',NULL,'white','female','Barbara A. Favola represents Virginia Senate District 40 as a Democrat, and took office in January 2012. Favola graduated from Saint Joseph\'s College in West Hartford, Connecticut, and earned her Master of Public Administration from New York University in 1980. She served as a Presidential Management Intern and rose to Senior Advisor in the Department of Health and Human Services, where she worked for fifteen years. Favola was elected to the Arlington County Board in 1997 and served for fourteen years, including three terms as chairwoman. She chairs the Senate Rehabilitation and Social Services Committee and serves on the Finance and Appropriations, Courts of Justice, Rules, and Education and Health committees. She resides in Arlington with her husband, Doug Weik.','2011-12-29 23:00:16','2026-01-06 02:11:30'),
(377,'krkrupicka','Krupicka, Rob','K. Robert Krupicka, Jr.','1971-02-18','white','male','This California native holds a degree in economics from the University of Virginia. A communications and business strategy consultant, he is married with two children.','2013-01-07 00:00:00','2020-02-15 02:19:18'),
