(403,'jsmcpike','McPike, Jeremy','Jeremy S. McPike',NULL,'white','male','Jeremy S. McPike represents Virginia Senate District 29 as a Democrat, and took office in January 2016. McPike resides in Prince William County.','2016-01-07 02:38:27','2026-01-06 02:11:30'),
(404,'ghsturtevant','Sturtevant, Glen','Glen H. Sturtevant, Jr.',NULL,'white','male','Glen H. Sturtevant represents Virginia Senate District 13 as a Republican, and took office in January 2024. Born in Spotsylvania County, Sturtevant earned his law degree from George Mason University\'s Antonin Scalia School of Law, where he served as an editor for the law school\'s legal journal. He practices as an attorney representing veterans and their family members. Sturtevant served on the Richmond School Board and was elected to the Virginia Senate in 2015, serving until 2020, before being re-elected in 2024. He resides in Midlothian with his wife, Lori, and their four children.','2016-01-07 02:45:43','2026-01-06 02:11:30'),
(405,'drsuetterlein','Suetterlein, David','David R. Suetterlein',NULL,'white','male','David R. Suetterlein represents Virginia Senate District 4 as a Republican, and took office in January 2016. Born in 1985, Suetterlein graduated from Grove City College with a Bachelor of Arts. He resides in Roanoke County.','2016-01-07 02:52:39','2026-01-06 02:11:30'),
(406,'ldaird','Aird, Lashrecse','Lashrecse D. Aird',NULL,'black','female','Lashrecse D. Aird represents Virginia Senate District 13 as a Democrat, and took office in January 2024. Born in Buffalo, New York, in 1986, Aird earned a Bachelor of Arts from Virginia State University. She serves as Executive Director of the Virginia State University & Richard Bland College Joint School of Professional and Technical Studies and served in the Virginia House of Delegates from 2016 to 2022 before her election to the Senate. She resides in Petersburg with her husband, Blaine.','2016-01-07 02:59:06','2026-01-06 02:11:30'),
(407,'lbagby','Bagby, Lamont','Lamont Bagby',NULL,'black','male','Lamont Bagby represents Virginia Senate District 14 as a Democrat, and took office in January 2016. Born in Richmond in 1976, Bagby earned a Bachelor of Science in Business Education from Norfolk State University and a Master of Education in Educational Leadership from Virginia Commonwealth University. He served in the Virginia House of Delegates from 2015 to 2023 before his election to the Senate. He resides in Richmond with his wife, Jevata.','2016-01-09 02:42:52','2026-01-06 02:11:30'),
