(540,'tbmulchi','Mulchi, Tammy','Tammy Brankley Mulchi',NULL,'white','female','Tammy Brankley Mulchi represents Virginia Senate District 9 as a Republican, and took office in January 2024. Born in South Hill in 1966, Mulchi attended Liberty University. She works as a realtor and residential contractor and is founder and president of The Windsong Foundation. She resides in Mecklenburg County with her husband, Randy.','2024-01-11 03:36:16','2026-01-06 02:11:31'),
(541,'jjsingh','Singh, JJ','JJ Singh',NULL,NULL,NULL,'JJ Singh represents Virginia House District 26 as a Democrat, and took office in January 2025. The son of immigrants, Singh was born and raised in Northern Virginia. He served in the Peace Corps in Bolivia and worked as a senior advisor in the U.S. Senate. He operates his own business and resides in Loudoun County with his wife and their two daughters.','2025-01-08 02:18:10','2026-02-13 17:42:24'),
(542,'lhcifers','Cifers, Luther','Luther Cifers',NULL,'white','male','Luther H. Cifers represents Virginia Senate District 10 as a Republican, and took office in January 2025. Born in Richmond in 1974, Cifers earned an Associate degree in General Studies from Southside Virginia Community College. He works as an entrepreneur and resides in Buckingham County with his wife, Anastasia.','2025-01-19 03:33:40','2026-01-06 02:11:30'),
