(324,'Albert C. Pollard, Jr.','Pollard, Albert','Del. Albert Pollard (D-Lively)','acpollard','pollard','house',99,'2008-02-20','2012-01-10','D','Pollard held the seat from 2000-2005 before stepping down and running (unsuccessfully) for state senate, though regained his seat after his replacement won election to the U.S. House of Representatives.\r\n\r\nHe holds a degree in urban planning from Virginia Commonwealth University. Pollard is married and has three young children.','1967-09-18','white','male','',NULL,'804-698-1099','PO Box 508, Lively, VA 22507',NULL,'DelAPollard@house.virginia.gov','http://www.albertpollard.com/','http://www.problemsofparallax.com/feeds/posts/defaul',NULL,NULL,'132','Lively',NULL,63,'2020-02-15 02:19:18','2008-02-20 19:10:46'),
(325,'Rev. Delores L. McQuinn','McQuinn, Delores','Del. Delores McQuinn (D-Richmond)','dlmcquinn','mcquinn','house',401,'2009-01-14',NULL,'D','McQuinn studied at Virginia Commonwealth University and Virginia Union University. She is an associate minister at Mount Olivet Baptist Church in Richmond. Previously a member of the Richmond City Council and the Richmond School Board, McQuinn was elected to the House in a special election after Del. Dwight Jones was elected Richmond mayor.',NULL,'white','male',NULL,'804-698-1081','804-698-1081','P.O. Box 406 Richmond, VA 23218','914','DelDMcQuinn@house.virginia.gov',NULL,NULL,NULL,'PP-12-01023','207','Richmond','O:8:\"stdClass\":1:{s:4:\"List\";N;}',22,'2025-12-04 19:00:31','2009-01-08 22:48:41'),
(326,'Barry D. Knight','Knight, Barry','Del. Barry Knight (R-Virginia Beach)','bdknight','knight','house',418,'2009-01-14',NULL,'R','The owner and operator of Barry D. Knight Farms (a hog farm), Knight, his wife, and three children live in Pungo. Knight won his seat in a special election following the resignation of Del. Terrie Suit.','1954-09-26','white','male',NULL,'757-426-6387','804-698-1098','1852 Mill Landing Road Virginia Beach, VA 23457','809','DelBKnight@house.virginia.gov',NULL,NULL,'BarryKnight81','CC-12-00548','206','Virginia Beach','O:8:\"stdClass\":1:{s:4:\"List\";N;}',71,'2025-12-06 17:41:55','2009-01-08 22:53:00'),
(327,'Charniele L. Herring','Herring, Charniele','Del. Charniele Herring (D-Alexandria)','clherring','herring','house',324,'2009-01-26',NULL,'D','An attorney and government contractor, Del. Herring was elected in a special election after Del. Brian Moran stepped down from the seat to run for governor. She earned a BA in Economics from George Mason University and a JD from Catholic University',NULL,'white','male',NULL,'703-606-9705','804-698-1004','P.O. Box 11779 Alexandria, VA 22312','140','DelCHerring@house.virginia.gov',NULL,NULL,'C_Herring','CC-12-01191','208','Alexandria','O:8:\"stdClass\":1:{s:4:\"List\";N;}',24,'2025-12-06 17:43:12','2009-01-27 17:37:12'),
